$internal
$no.symbols
$no.xref
function py_initialize()
$catalog !py_initialize

$include KEYS.H

deffun PY_IS_INITIALIZED() calling '!PY_IS_INITIALIZED'

* 12 Sep 26 Windows port - THE NEWLINE RECONFIGURE IS GONE.  RELEASE_1.1 22.
*
* It ran a three-line script after a successful init:
*
*   import sys
*   sys.stderr.reconfigure(newline='\r\n')
*   sys.stdout.reconfigure(newline='\r\n')
*
* ***IT THREW EVERY TIME AND MADE A GOOD INIT REPORT -12004.***  Measured on
* the 22:55:41 install: PY_INITIALIZE returned -12004 while PY_IS_INITIALIZED
* answered 1 and every later call worked.
*
* reconfigure() is a TextIOWrapper method.  sdpy.c:231 replaces sys.stdout and
* sys.stderr with an io.StringIO BEFORE ANY USER CODE CAN RUN, and that is a
* requirement of the helper shape rather than a detail: stdout IS the protocol
* channel, so a script that printed would corrupt the frame stream.  StringIO
* has no reconfigure - measured, AttributeError - so the FIRST line threw and
* the other two never ran.
*
* SO NOTHING IS LOST BY REMOVING IT.  The translation it asked for has not
* happened since the interpreter moved out of sd.exe; it was already dead, and
* only the status code was wrong.  Output now comes back as payload through
* the protocol, so line endings are the caller's business at this end.

* skip initialize if already so
if py_is_initialized() then
  rtnstat = 0
end else
  rtnstat = SDEXT('',@FALSE,SD_PyInit)
end
return rtnstat

end
